            <h1 class="detail-title">Grant writing automation</h1>
            <p class="detail-subtitle">Pre-fill repeat-heavy grant applications with your organisation’s information so teams stop retyping the same material.</p>

            <div class="detail-body">
                <h3>The problem</h3>
                <p>Grant applications often consume an entire day because teams keep copying the same organisational information into different forms, checking wording for consistency, and reformatting material over and over again.</p>

                <h3>The solution</h3>
                <p>This system stores core information once and uses it to produce draft applications automatically. Teams can focus on the parts that actually need judgement: the project, the framing, and the funding case.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Stores key organisational information in one place</li>
                    <li>Matches project requirements with suitable funders</li>
                    <li>Creates pre-filled draft applications for review</li>
                    <li>Maintains consistency across submissions</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Results</h3>
                <p>Eight hours can be reduced to around ten minutes per application. For organisations completing multiple applications each year, that creates meaningful fundraising capacity without adding staff hours.</p>

                <h3>Best fit</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Charities and social enterprises applying for several grants per year</li>
                    <li>Teams with limited fundraising capacity</li>
                    <li>Organisations that want more consistency across applications</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
